<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI12-QA1-BLOCKING-03>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI12-QA1-BLOCKING-03" ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-Legacy ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-22T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:title "Rewritten AST boundary test cannot detect the BLOCKING-01/02 leaks; does not validly close AI11-BLOCKING-03-POSTWRITEROUTER-NOOP" ;
  triage:description "The rewritten canonical_write_router_has_one_host_routing_decision test (introduced in pAI-s12-post-write-router, a8ea0017) uses an AST visitor to enforce AI.12 routing constraints. However, the visitor's violation detection logic gates all violations behind is_runtime_dispatcher_source() || source_path.is_none(), which means violations in canonical write modules other than runtime_health.rs are silently dropped. Violations in crates/atm-core/src/send/mod.rs where BLOCKING-01 exists will not be caught. Additionally, the negative fixtures test (canonical_write_router_rejects_all_mandated_negative_fixtures) only exercises the fixture validation helper; it does not confirm that the main test would reject actual production violations. The sprint doc mandates that AST-based boundary tests must scan all files in the canonical write path, record all occurrences, and provide negative fixture validation. This test does neither for files outside runtime_health.rs." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "crate" ;
  triage:category "QA-BLOCKING" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI12-QA1-BLOCKING-03/s12/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI12-QA1-BLOCKING-03/s13/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI12-QA1-BLOCKING-03/s14/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI12-QA1-BLOCKING-03/s15/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI12-QA1-BLOCKING-03/s16/1> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s12/a8ea0017> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s13/2adc5fa1> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s14/ef0e5e2b> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s15/5a7a762f> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s16/1c23ac04> ;
  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s16/1c23ac04> ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-22T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:correctionNote "2026-07-26 (quality-mgr): independently re-verified at integrate/phase-AI tip against arch-ctm's legacy close/waive batch recommendation -- still OPEN, not eligible for close/waive. crates/atm-architecture/tests/boundary_enforcement.rs canonical_write_router_has_one_host_routing_decision() (line 308) does scan every .rs file under crates/ via canonical_write_modules()/collect_rust_files(), so delivery_policy.rs is included. But HostRoutingVisitor::visit_expr_method_call's peer-delivery classification is still gated behind is_runtime_dispatcher_source() (used at line 715) and equivalent per-callsite provenance checks -- the same narrow gating this finding originally flagged. This is consistent with AI12-QA1-BLOCKING-01 remaining open (delivery_policy.rs's independent host check at line 349 is a live violation the visitor does not attribute as a second PostWriteRouter-equivalent decision point). Confirmed via direct code read, not self-report." .

